course: dictionary
lesson: 3996
title: Gambling: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the author means. «Loot boxes work like gambling, because you pay money for a random chance at a prize.» Here you pay money and do not know what you will get, so gambling means betting money on something that luck decides.
explain: Now read «Gambling with someone's safety.» Nobody is betting money here, so the clue is the word safety. Gambling here means taking a big risk in the hope that things will turn out well. Always ask: does the sentence talk about money, or about risk?
explain: Context can also tell you that gambling is for grown-ups. «Gambling is against the law under 18» means children must never do it. Gambling can become a harmful habit, called a gambling addiction, so when a word matters this much, a grown-up you trust is the best person to ask.
fact: Gambling means playing games or betting money on something where luck decides the result.
fact: Gambling can also mean taking a big risk in the hope that things turn out well.
fact: «Gambling is against the law under 18», so children must never gamble.
fact: The chances of winning are usually small, and the house usually wins.
fact: «Gambling addiction» means a person keeps betting to win back losses; doctors and charities can help.
exercise: «Loot boxes work like gambling, because you pay money for a random chance at a prize.» What does gambling mean here? | Practising the piano every day | Paying money for a chance, where luck decides what you get | Saving coins in a jar | *Betting money on something where luck decides the result
exercise: In «gambling with someone's safety», what is gambling closest to? | Keeping a secret | Playing a board game with friends | *Taking a big risk | Sharing money equally
exercise: Why does the sentence «Gambling is against the law under 18» tell us something important? | *Gambling is for grown-ups, and children must not do it | Children are the best at gambling | Children can gamble if a parent says yes | Gambling is always free
test: In «Gambling addiction means a person keeps betting to win back losses», what are losses? | *Money or games lost | Songs sung | Friends made | Prizes won
test: In «Mia gambled her pocket money on a machine», what does gambled mean? | Saved carefully | *Bet on luck to try to win more | Counted slowly | Lent to a friend
exam: Which phrase uses gambling to mean taking a big risk? | «gambling problem» | *«gambling with someone's safety» | «online gambling» | «gambling machine»
